# Data comparison across dimensions rejected

Verifies a comparison between incompatible measure dimensions is rejected at compile time. A kilobyte and a meter belong to separate dimensions with no registered comparison rule, so the compiler reports the undefined operand pair instead of scaling across dimensions.

>>> source
size: int = 1KB
print(size == 1m)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: comparison `==` is not defined for `int64[KB]` and `int64[m]` at Span { start: 22, end: 32 }

<<< exit
1
